flag(28,'distractors','Retaining12 pairs after only8 calls is impossible from the premise, while the other wrong options redefine entries as tokens or arbitrarily reset the counter. Use plausible retained pair counts, earliest retained exchange and independent lifetime counter errors.')
flag(32,'assumptions answerSet','Each offered result omits the required explanation string. The intended numeric/label tuple is valid, but no listed object satisfies the complete EmotionAnalysis schema as written. State that all results also contain a valid explanation and only these four fields are compared, or include it in every option.')
flag(33,'distractors','User deception and a physiological certainty inference from a service failure are implausible. Use realistic fallback-handling alternatives such as retaining prior state, treating missing output as a confident neutral observation, and distinguishing diagnostic failure from successful classification.')
flag(35,'distractors','Synthesizing an observed cue before it is sensed and treating an estimated label itself as an expressive action are weak. Use parallel real recognition/synthesis operations, ideally a sensor-to-policy-to-output scenario.')
flag(36,'distractors','The wrong alternatives assert perfect universal accuracy, direct hidden-state access or no need for labels/evaluation. Use plausible alternative evaluation interpretations, such as observer agreement, cross-subject held-out performance and training-set accuracy.')
flag(38,'sourceSupport','The sole slide shows a loop through a Test FER Model box; it does not explicitly supply the validation/untouched-test remedy being tested. Preserve the source conflict and add primary implementation/evaluation evidence for this explanatory correction, such as the official scikit-learn cross-validation section on validation selection versus final test evaluation. Do not present the remedy as a literal slide statement.')
